# Only files the image build actually consumes are sent to the build context.
#
# Start from "exclude everything", then allow exactly the inputs the Dockerfile
# copies. The fork's tree also holds tests, documentation and agent state that no
# layer needs, so an allowlist keeps the context small and makes a missing build
# input fail loudly instead of shipping silently.
#
# `.env.railway` must survive this file. docker-entrypoint.sh loads it as the boot
# fallback for a standalone deploy, and the runtime stage copies it out of the
# builder. Upstream's `.env*` rule dropped it silently, which failed the build at
# `COPY --from=builder /build/.env.railway`. It holds no secret: the key in it is
# a placeholder the entrypoint refuses to start on.
*
!Dockerfile
!docker-entrypoint.sh
!.env.railway
!package.json
!bun.lock
!tsconfig.json
!dashboard/package.json
!src
!scripts
!migrations
!dashboard

# Never ship local secrets, caches, or build output. The `*` rule above already
# excludes these; they are named so the intent survives a change to that rule.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
node_modules
node_modules/**
**/node_modules
**/node_modules/**
**/dist
**/*.test.ts
.git
.git/**
